@* Cart.razor — Phase 4.1

   Customer-facing shopping cart page at route `/Cart`. All authenticated
   users except ReadOnly can shop (the MainLayout already gates the sidebar
   link — Customer + Admin/Manager/Employee see it, ReadOnly doesn't).

   BACKEND CONTRACT:
     - Load:    GetActiveCartForUserQuery → Result<CartDto?>
       - Success(null)  = empty cart (normal state, not an error)
       - Success(CartDto) = cart with line items + live stock per line
       - Failure(error)  = load failed (auth, DB timeout, etc.)
     - Update qty:   UpdateSaleLineItemCommand(SaleId, LineItemId, Quantity) → Result
     - Remove line:  RemoveSaleLineItemCommand(SaleId, LineItemId) → Result
     - Clear cart:   DeleteDraftSaleCommand(SaleId) → Result
     - Submit cart:  SubmitSaleCommand(SaleId) → Result
   All five go through Wolverine's IMessageBus.InvokeAsync, which routes
   them through the auth + logging + performance middleware pipeline
   (same as every other command/query in the app).

   LAYOUT (responsive):
     Desktop / tablet (≥992px): two columns
       Left  (8/12): line-item list (each item = picture + info + qty + actions)
       Right (4/12): sticky summary panel (totals + submit + clear + continue)
     Mobile (<992px): single column, summary collapses to bottom

   STATES:
     1. Loading       — spinner while the cart query resolves
     2. Error         — alert with the error message + retry button
     3. Empty cart    — friendly empty-state with "Browse products" CTA
     4. Cart with items — the main shopping cart surface (the bulk of this file)

   PER-LINE STOCK BADGE:
     Each line shows a small badge reflecting the relationship between the
     line's Quantity and the live Product.StockQuantity (CurrentStock on
     the DTO):
       - In stock (green)         — CurrentStock ≥ Quantity and > 0
       - Low stock (orange)       — 0 < CurrentStock < Quantity
       - Out of stock (red)       — CurrentStock == 0
     The badge is informational — the user can still click Update (the
     backend will reject with a friendly message). But the SUBMIT button
     is disabled if ANY line has stock issues, so the user must fix them
     before checking out.

   QTY SELECTOR:
     RadzenNumeric with Min=1, Max=Math.Max(CurrentStock, Quantity).
     The unusual Max formula lets the user KEEP an over-stock quantity
     (so they can deliberately reduce it) without forcing them to first
     drop to CurrentStock. But they can't INCREASE past CurrentStock.

   CLEAR CART CONFIRMATION:
     We use an INLINE confirmation pattern (toggle a bool flag, show
     Yes/No buttons in place of the Clear button) rather than a JS
     confirm() dialog. Inline confirmation is more accessible (works
     with screen readers, doesn't depend on browser dialog styling)
     and matches the Radzen visual language.

   SUBMIT FLOW:
     On success: show a success toast, then navigate to /Sales (the
     user's order history — Phase 4.2 will build this page; for now
     the route exists only as a placeholder, but navigating there is
     still better than leaving them on an empty cart). We do NOT
     reload the cart here — the cart is now in Pending status, so
     GetActiveCartForUserQuery will return null on next load anyway.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings go through IStringLocalizer<Cart> (Loc).
     Money is formatted via FormatPrice() (same helper as ProductDetail
     and Products) — keeps the visual language consistent.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All button clicks are async event handlers
     that dispatch commands via Wolverine. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery
     token is established at circuit start. *@

@page "/Cart"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Errors
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Queries.GetActiveCartForUser
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.UpdateSaleLineItem
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.RemoveSaleLineItem
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.DeleteDraftSale
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.SubmitSale
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Components.CartBudgetBar
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<Cart> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Two-column layout: line items left, summary right.
                                               On tablet/mobile, summary collapses below the items. */
            .cart-layout {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 1.5rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .cart-layout {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                }
            }

            /* ── Line item card ──
                                               Each line item is its own RadzenCard with a grid layout:
                                                 [picture] [info] [qty + actions]
                                               On mobile, the picture shrinks and the layout collapses to
                                               a vertical stack with actions wrapping below. */
            .cart-line {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: 80px minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
                gap: 1rem;
                align-items: center;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 600px) {
                .cart-line {
                    grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr);
                    grid-template-rows: auto auto;
                    gap: 0.75rem;
                }

                    .cart-line .cart-line-actions {
                        grid-column: 1 / -1;
                        justify-content: space-between;
                    }
            }

            .cart-line .cart-line-picture {
                aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                overflow: hidden;
            }

                .cart-line .cart-line-picture img {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .cart-line .cart-line-picture .rz-icon {
                    font-size: 2.5rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

            .cart-line .cart-line-name {
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 1rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                text-decoration: none;
                display: block;
                line-height: 1.3;
            }

                .cart-line .cart-line-name:hover {
                    color: var(--rz-primary);
                    text-decoration: underline;
                }

            .cart-line .cart-line-unit-price {
                font-size: 0.85rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin-top: 0.15rem;
            }

            .cart-line .cart-line-total {
                font-weight: 700;
                color: var(--rz-primary);
                margin-top: 0.25rem;
            }

            .cart-line .cart-line-actions {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            /* Qty selector — a plain <input type="number" class="rz-textbox qty-input">
                                       rather than a RadzenNumeric. WHY: RadzenNumeric's internal JS
                                       mishandles caret position in RTL (fa-IR) mode — the cursor looks
                                       like it's at the end of the value, but typing inserts the
                                       character at the BEGINNING (turning a "1" + typed "0" into "01"
                                       instead of "10"). A native input with dir="ltr" bypasses
                                       Radzen's JS entirely and handles caret position AND character
                                       insertion correctly in both LTR and RTL page contexts. Same fix
                                       as CreateProduct.razor's PriceAmount / InitialStockQuantity
                                       fields. We lose the spinner arrows but gain correct behavior. */
            .cart-line .qty-input {
                width: 90px;
                text-align: left;
            }

            /* Stock badge — same visual language as ProductDetail.razor */
            .stock-badge {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.3rem;
                padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
                border-radius: 9999px;
                font-size: 0.75rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                margin-top: 0.25rem;
            }

            .stock-in {
                background: rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.15);
                color: #4caf50;
            }

            .stock-low {
                background: rgba(255, 152, 0, 0.15);
                color: #ff9800;
            }

            .stock-out {
                background: rgba(244, 67, 54, 0.15);
                color: #f44336;
            }

            /* Summary panel — sticky on desktop so it stays in view while
                                               the user scrolls long carts. On mobile it just sits at the
                                               bottom of the page (no sticky — would cover content). */
            .cart-summary {
                position: sticky;
                top: 1rem;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .cart-summary {
                    position: static;
                }
            }

            .cart-summary-row {
                display: flex;
                justify-content: space-between;
                align-items: baseline;
                padding: 0.5rem 0;
            }

                .cart-summary-row .label {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    font-size: 0.95rem;
                }

                .cart-summary-row .value {
                    font-weight: 600;
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                }

                .cart-summary-row.total-row {
                    border-top: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                    margin-top: 0.5rem;
                    padding-top: 1rem;
                }

                    .cart-summary-row.total-row .label {
                        font-size: 1.05rem;
                        font-weight: 600;
                        color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                    }

                    .cart-summary-row.total-row .value {
                        font-size: 1.5rem;
                        font-weight: 700;
                        color: var(--rz-primary);
                    }

            .cart-actions {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                margin-top: 1rem;
            }

            /* Empty state — centered icon + message + CTA */
            .cart-empty {
                text-align: center;
                padding: 3rem 1rem;
            }

                .cart-empty .cart-empty-icon {
                    font-size: 5rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    opacity: 0.5;
                    margin-bottom: 1rem;
                }

                .cart-empty .cart-empty-title {
                    font-size: 1.4rem;
                    font-weight: 700;
                    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                }

                .cart-empty .cart-empty-message {
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
                    max-width: 400px;
                    margin-left: auto;
                    margin-right: auto;
                }

            /* Page header — title + item count badge */
            .cart-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }

                .cart-header .cart-header-icon {
                    font-size: 1.75rem;
                    color: var(--rz-primary);
                }

                .cart-header .cart-header-title {
                    font-size: 1.5rem;
                    font-weight: 700;
                    margin: 0;
                }

                .cart-header .cart-count-badge {
                    background: var(--rz-primary);
                    color: var(--rz-primary-foreground-color, #fff);
                    border-radius: 9999px;
                    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
                    font-size: 0.85rem;
                    font-weight: 600;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1.25rem">
    @* ── Page header ──
       Title + cart icon + item-count badge (only when cart has items). *@
    <div class="cart-header">
        <RadzenIcon Icon="shopping_cart" class="cart-header-icon" />
        <h1 class="cart-header-title">@Loc["PageHeading"]</h1>
        @if (_cart is not null && _cart.LineItems.Count > 0)
        {
            var liveItemCount = ComputeTotalItemCount();
            <span class="cart-count-badge">
                @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                    liveItemCount == 1 ? Loc["ItemCountSingular"] : Loc["ItemCount"],
                    liveItemCount)
            </span>
        }
    </div>

    @* ── Monthly budget bar (Step 7) ──
       Renders ABOVE the loading/error/empty/items branches so it's visible
       in every cart state EXCEPT "loading" and "error" (when we don't yet
       have authoritative budget info to show).

       WHEN NULL:
         GetActiveCartForUserQueryHandler populates BudgetInfo as null when:
           - The user is staff (no GroupId) → staff don't have a salary budget
           - The system's LimitMode is CountOnly → budget not enforced
         In both cases the bar is hidden — correct UX.

       WHEN POPULATED + EMPTY CART:
         The customer has no active draft but DOES have a salary budget
         (e.g. they've submitted an order earlier this month). The bar
         shows their monthly budget, what they've already spent, and what
         remains — encouraging them to start a new cart.

       WHEN POPULATED + CART WITH ITEMS:
         The bar shows the live status. CartTotal is the LIVE pending-qty
         total (ComputeCartTotal), not the server's _cart.Total — this
         keeps the bar in sync with the user's typing in the qty selectors
         even before they click Update. The bar's Remaining value comes
         from the server's snapshot (Budget.Remaining), which already
         includes the server's cart total via the "cart reserves budget"
         rule. So as the user types a larger quantity, the bar's
         "Remaining" stays at the server's value (doesn't change live),
         but the "In cart now" row updates to reflect the typed quantity.
         This is intentional: the bar's authoritative numbers come from
         the server; the live "In cart now" is a UX affordance showing
         "if you commit this, this is how much your cart will be". The
         numbers reconcile after the next LoadCartAsync call.

       LIVE UPDATES:
         The bar re-renders on every keystroke in the qty selector (via
         CartTotal = ComputeCartTotal() which reads _pendingQuantities).
         No backend round-trip until the user commits (blur / Enter). On
         commit, LoadCartAsync refreshes _cart + _cart.BudgetInfo from
         the server, which gives the bar its new authoritative values. *@
    @if (_cart?.BudgetInfo is not null)
    {
        <CartBudgetBar Budget="_cart.BudgetInfo" CartTotal="ComputeCartTotal()" />
    }

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                      Icon="refresh"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                      Click="@LoadCartAsync" />
    }

    @* ── Empty cart ── *@
    else if (_cart is null || _cart.LineItems.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <div class="cart-empty">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="remove_shopping_cart" class="cart-empty-icon" />
                <div class="cart-empty-title">@Loc["EmptyTitle"]</div>
                <p class="cart-empty-message">@Loc["EmptyMessage"]</p>
                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BrowseProductsButton"]"
                              Icon="inventory_2"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
            </div>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Cart with items ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="cart-layout">
            @* LEFT — line items list *@
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="0.75rem">
                @foreach (var line in _cart.LineItems)
                {
                    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1rem;">
                        <div class="cart-line">
                            @* Picture (clickable → product detail page) *@
                            <a href="@($"/Products/{line.ProductId}")" class="cart-line-picture" aria-label="@line.ProductName">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" />
                            </a>

                            @* Info: name (link) + unit price + line total + stock badge *@
                            <div>
                                <a href="@($"/Products/{line.ProductId}")" class="cart-line-name">@line.ProductName</a>
                                <div class="cart-line-unit-price">
                                    @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["UnitPriceLabel"], FormatPrice(line.UnitPrice))
                                </div>
                                <div class="cart-line-total">@FormatPrice(ComputeLineTotal(line))</div>
                                @if (line.CurrentStock == 0)
                                {
                                    <span class="stock-badge stock-out">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="error_outline" />
                                        @Loc["StockOut"]
                                    </span>
                                }
                                else if (line.CurrentStock < line.Quantity)
                                {
                                    <span class="stock-badge stock-low">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="warning_amber" />
                                        @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["StockLow"], line.CurrentStock)
                                    </span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span class="stock-badge stock-in">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="check_circle" />
                                        @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["StockIn"], line.CurrentStock)
                                    </span>
                                }
                            </div>

                            @* Actions: qty selector + remove.
                               NO Update button — qty changes are saved on blur
                               via OnQtyCommitAsync. The displayed line total +
                               cart total + item count update LIVE on every
                               keystroke (via @oninput + ComputeLineTotal /
                               ComputeCartTotal / ComputeTotalItemCount) so the
                               user sees the new price without clicking anything. *@
                            <div class="cart-line-actions">
                                @* Plain HTML <input type="number"> instead of RadzenNumeric.
                                   Same RTL caret-position fix as CreateProduct.razor's
                                   PriceAmount / InitialStockQuantity fields and
                                   RestockProductDialog.razor's Quantity input.
                                   RadzenNumeric's internal JS mishandles caret position
                                   in fa-IR mode — the cursor looks correct but typed
                                   characters insert at the BEGINNING ("1" + "0" → "01").
                                   The native input with dir="ltr" handles caret AND
                                   insertion correctly. We lose the spinner arrows but
                                   gain correct behavior.

                                   LIVE PRICE UPDATES:
                                   @oninput fires on every keystroke → OnQtyInput parses +
                                   clamps + stores in _pendingQuantities → UI re-renders
                                   with updated line total + cart total. NO backend call.

                                   BACKEND SAVE ON BLUR:
                                   @onchange fires when the user tabs / clicks away (or
                                   presses Enter) → OnQtyCommitAsync parses + clamps +
                                   stores, then if the resulting qty differs from the
                                   server's line.Quantity, dispatches
                                   UpdateSaleLineItemCommand. On failure, the cart is
                                   reloaded which reverts the displayed qty. So the DB
                                   is touched at most once per editing session, never on
                                   every keystroke.

                                   Upper-bound clamping that RadzenNumeric's Max attribute
                                   used to provide is now done in OnQtyInput /
                                   OnQtyCommitAsync (the native input's max attribute only
                                   constrains the spinner, not what the user can type). *@
                                <input type="number"
                                       class="rz-textbox qty-input"
                                       dir="ltr"
                                       step="1"
                                       min="1"
                                       max="@GetLineMax(line)"
                                       value="@GetPendingQty(line.Id)"
                                       disabled="@_isBusy"
                                       @oninput="@(e => OnQtyInput(line, e.Value))"
                                       @onchange="@(e => OnQtyCommitAsync(line, e.Value))"
                                       aria-label="@Loc["QuantityLabel"]" />
                                <RadzenButton Icon="delete"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              Title="@Loc["RemoveButton"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["RemoveButton"]"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@(() => HandleRemoveLineAsync(line.Id))" />
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </RadzenCard>
                }

                @* Continue Shopping — sits below the line items list (left column,
                   matches Amazon's cart pattern). Style (ButtonStyle.Secondary +
                   Variant.Outlined) matches the Sales page's Continue Shopping
                   button so the two pages share a consistent visual language.
                   align-self: flex-start shrinks the button to fit its content —
                   by default RadzenStack (flex column) stretches children to full
                   width, which made this button span the entire left column. *@
                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ContinueShoppingButton"]"
                              Icon="arrow_back"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                              Style="align-self: flex-start;"
                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
            </RadzenStack>

            @* RIGHT — sticky summary panel *@
            <div class="cart-summary">
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["SummaryTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;" />

                    <div class="cart-summary-row">
                        <span class="label">@Loc["TotalItems"]</span>
                        <span class="value">
                            @{
                                var liveItemCount = ComputeTotalItemCount();
                            }
                            @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                                liveItemCount == 1 ? Loc["ItemCountSingular"] : Loc["ItemCount"],
                                liveItemCount)
                        </span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="cart-summary-row">
                        <span class="label">@Loc["LineItemsCount"]</span>
                        <span class="value">
                            @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                                _cart.LineItems.Count == 1 ? Loc["ItemCountSingular"] : Loc["ItemCount"],
                                _cart.LineItems.Count)
                        </span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="cart-summary-row total-row">
                        <span class="label">@Loc["TotalAmount"]</span>
                        <span class="value">@FormatPrice(ComputeCartTotal())</span>
                    </div>

                    @if (HasStockIssue())
                    {
                        <RadzenAlert Text="@Loc["StockIssueWarning"]"
                                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                     ShowIcon="true"
                                     Style="margin-top: 1rem;" />
                    }
                    @if (HasLimitIssue())
                    {
                        <RadzenAlert Text="@Loc["LimitIssueWarning"]"
                                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                     ShowIcon="true"
                                     Style="margin-top: 1rem;" />
                    }

                    <div class="cart-actions">
                        @if (_confirmingClear)
                        {
                            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="0.4rem">
                                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["ConfirmClearMessage"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2" />
                                <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" Gap="0.5rem">
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ConfirmClearYes"]"
                                                  Icon="delete_forever"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                                  Click="@HandleClearCartAsync" />
                                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ConfirmClearNo"]"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                  Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                                  Click="@(() => _confirmingClear = false)" />
                                </RadzenStack>
                            </RadzenStack>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["SubmitCartButton"]"
                                          Icon="shopping_cart_checkout"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Style="width: 100%;"
                                          Disabled="@(_isBusy || HasStockIssue() || HasLimitIssue())"
                                          Click="@HandleSubmitCartAsync" />
                            @* Clear Cart — matches the UserDetail page's Deactivate
                               button style (ButtonStyle.Danger + Variant.Outlined) so
                               destructive secondary actions share a consistent visual
                               language across the app. Icon stays as delete_sweep. *@
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ClearCartButton"]"
                                          Icon="delete_sweep"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Style="width: 100%;"
                                          Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                          Click="@(() => _confirmingClear = true)" />
                        }
                    </div>
                </RadzenCard>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private CartDto? _cart;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// True during any mutation (update/remove/clear/submit). Disables ALL
    /// action buttons + qty selectors so the user can't fire concurrent
    /// commands at the same line (which could race against each other and
    /// leave the cart in an inconsistent state).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isBusy;

    /// <summary>
    /// Tracks user input in the qty selectors BEFORE they click "Update".
    /// Keyed by line item Id. Initialized from line.Quantity when the cart
    /// loads; updated live as the user types; reset back to line.Quantity
    /// after a successful Update (because the cart is reloaded).
    /// </summary>
    private readonly Dictionary<Guid, int> _pendingQuantities = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Toggles the inline "Are you sure?" confirmation for the Clear button.
    /// Replaces the Clear + Submit buttons with Yes/No buttons while true.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _confirmingClear;

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await LoadCartAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadCartAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<CartDto?>>(new GetActiveCartForUserQuery());

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _cart = result.Value;
                _loadError = null;

                // Re-seed pending-qty state from the freshly-loaded cart.
                // Existing entries for line items that no longer exist (e.g.
                // after a remove) are pruned.
                _pendingQuantities.Clear();
                if (_cart is not null)
                {
                    foreach (var line in _cart.LineItems)
                    {
                        _pendingQuantities[line.Id] = line.Quantity;
                    }
                }

                // Reset the clear-confirm state — if the cart was just
                // cleared, the confirmation UI should not linger.
                _confirmingClear = false;
            }
            else
            {
                _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Defensive — any unexpected exception (Wolverine timeout, etc.).
            // Don't leak exception details to the UI.
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
    }

    // ── Mutation handlers ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleUpdateLineAsync(Guid lineItemId)
    {
        if (_cart is null || _isBusy) return;

        // Read the pending qty; if not in the dictionary (defensive — shouldn't
        // happen), fall back to the current line quantity.
        if (!_pendingQuantities.TryGetValue(lineItemId, out var newQty)) return;
        if (newQty < 1) return;

        _isBusy = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new UpdateSaleLineItemCommand(_cart.SaleId, lineItemId, newQty));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(Loc["Updated"], summary: Loc["UpdatedTitle"]);
                await LoadCartAsync(); // refresh from server — authoritative
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    LocalizeError(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_GenericUpdate"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
                // Reload to revert the pending qty back to the server's truth.
                await LoadCartAsync();
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericUpdate"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            await LoadCartAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleRemoveLineAsync(Guid lineItemId)
    {
        if (_cart is null || _isBusy) return;

        _isBusy = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new RemoveSaleLineItemCommand(_cart.SaleId, lineItemId));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(Loc["Removed"], summary: Loc["RemovedTitle"]);
                await LoadCartAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    LocalizeError(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_GenericRemove"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericRemove"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleClearCartAsync()
    {
        if (_cart is null || _isBusy) return;

        _isBusy = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeleteDraftSaleCommand(_cart.SaleId));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(Loc["Cleared"], summary: Loc["ClearedTitle"]);
                _confirmingClear = false;
                await LoadCartAsync(); // will show empty state
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    LocalizeError(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_GenericClear"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericClear"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleSubmitCartAsync()
    {
        if (_cart is null || _isBusy) return;

        // Defense-in-depth: even though the Submit button is disabled when
        // HasStockIssue / HasLimitIssue is true, the user could (via dev
        // tools) re-enable it. Re-check before dispatching.
        if (HasStockIssue())
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["StockIssueWarning"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }
        if (HasLimitIssue())
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["LimitIssueWarning"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        _isBusy = true;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new SubmitSaleCommand(_cart.SaleId));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(Loc["Submitted"], summary: Loc["SubmittedTitle"]);
                // Navigate to /Sales (the user's order history — Phase 4.2).
                // The submitted sale is now in Pending status, so reloading
                // /Cart would show the empty state.
                Navigation.NavigateTo("/Sales", forceLoad: false);
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    LocalizeError(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_GenericSubmit"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
                // Reload — the sale's state may have changed underneath us.
                await LoadCartAsync();
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["Error_GenericSubmit"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Pending-qty state helpers ──────────────────────────────────────

    private int GetPendingQty(Guid lineItemId)
        => _pendingQuantities.TryGetValue(lineItemId, out var q) ? q : 1;

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the upper bound for a cart line's quantity selector.
    ///
    /// Computed as: <c>Min(MyPurchaseLimit, Max(CurrentStock, Quantity))</c>.
    ///
    /// WHY Max(CurrentStock, Quantity) AND NOT JUST CurrentStock:
    ///   Same rationale as before this fix — if the live stock has dropped
    ///   below the line's current quantity (e.g. another customer bought
    ///   the last units while this cart was sitting open), we still let
    ///   the user SELECT their existing quantity so they can deliberately
    ///   reduce it. They just can't INCREASE past stock.
    ///
    /// WHY Min WITH MyPurchaseLimit:
    ///   Before this fix the limit was ignored entirely here, so a
    ///   customer could click + past their group's per-product limit and
    ///   only get stopped by a backend DomainException (surfaced as a
    ///   generic error toast). Clamping at the UI is the correct UX —
    ///   the customer can't even SELECT a quantity their group isn't
    ///   allowed to buy. For staff (MyPurchaseLimit == null), the limit
    ///   is omitted and the bound is just Max(CurrentStock, Quantity).
    /// </summary>
    private static int GetLineMax(CartLineItemDto line)
    {
        var byStock = Math.Max(line.CurrentStock, line.Quantity);
        return line.MyPurchaseLimit.HasValue
            ? Math.Min(line.MyPurchaseLimit.Value, byStock)
            : byStock;
    }

    private void SetPendingQty(Guid lineItemId, int value)
    {
        // Clamp to [1, ...] defensively. The upper bound (GetLineMax) is
        // enforced by OnQtyInput / OnQtyCommitAsync for the native
        // <input type="number"> qty selector (which has no built-in clamping
        // like RadzenNumeric's Max attribute used to provide). A programmatic
        // Set could still violate the upper bound, but the backend
        // UpdateSaleLineItemCommand rejects over-stock values as
        // defense-in-depth.
        if (value < 1) value = 1;
        _pendingQuantities[lineItemId] = value;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// @oninput handler for the qty selector. Fires on every keystroke.
    /// Parses the typed value, clamps it to the line's max, stores it in
    /// _pendingQuantities. NO backend call — the UI re-renders with the
    /// updated line total + cart total + item count from ComputeLineTotal /
    /// ComputeCartTotal / ComputeTotalItemCount (all read from
    /// _pendingQuantities), so the user sees the new price in real time
    /// without us touching the DB. The actual save happens on blur via
    /// OnQtyCommitAsync.
    ///
    /// CLAMPING IS VISIBLE TO THE USER:
    ///   Because the input's `value` attribute is one-way bound to
    ///   GetPendingQty(line.Id), Blazor's re-render after OnQtyInput runs
    ///   will overwrite whatever the user typed with the clamped value.
    ///   So if the user types "9" in a field where max is 5, the field
    ///   visually snaps back to "5" on the very next render. That's the
    ///   correct UX — the user can't even momentarily enter an invalid qty.
    ///
    /// INVALID INPUT:
    ///   HTML5 number inputs reject most non-numeric characters, so the only
    ///   realistic invalid case is the user clearing the field entirely. In
    ///   that case parse fails and we do nothing — _pendingQuantities stays
    ///   at the last valid value, the displayed total stays at the last
    ///   valid value, and the next @onchange (blur) will revert the field's
    ///   displayed value via the bound `value` attribute.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnQtyInput(CartLineItemDto line, object? rawValue)
    {
        if (rawValue is string s && int.TryParse(s, CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, out var parsed))
        {
            var max = GetLineMax(line);
            if (parsed > max) parsed = max;
            SetPendingQty(line.Id, parsed);
        }
        // else: invalid (empty / non-numeric) — leave _pendingQuantities
        // unchanged. The displayed line total + cart total stay at the last
        // valid value (since ComputeLineTotal / ComputeCartTotal read from
        // _pendingQuantities, not from the input's raw text).
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// @onchange handler for the qty selector. Fires when the user tabs /
    /// clicks away from the input (or presses Enter). Same parse + clamp +
    /// store as OnQtyInput, then if the resulting pending qty differs from
    /// the server's line.Quantity, dispatches UpdateSaleLineItemCommand to
    /// persist the change. On success or failure, the cart is reloaded —
    /// on success this confirms the new qty; on failure this reverts the
    /// displayed qty back to the server's truth.
    ///
    /// WHY @onchange AND NOT @oninput FOR THE SAVE:
    ///   @oninput fires on every keystroke. Saving on every keystroke would
    ///   spam the backend (one DB write per character typed — "1" → save,
    ///   "10" → save, "100" → save). @onchange fires once when the user is
    ///   done editing (blur / Enter), so we get at most one save per editing
    ///   session. The user explicitly asked for "no real-time DB writes" —
    ///   this is exactly that contract.
    ///
    /// WHY WE STILL RE-PARSE INSTEAD OF REUSING OnQtyInput's RESULT:
    ///   @onchange and @oninput both fire on the same keystroke that triggers
    ///   the change event (the blur happens after the last input). But the
    ///   raw value @onchange sees is the input's value AT THE TIME OF THE
    ///   CHANGE EVENT, which is the same as the last @oninput. Re-parsing is
    ///   cheap and keeps the two handlers independent — either can fire
    ///   without the other in edge cases (e.g. programmatic value changes).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task OnQtyCommitAsync(CartLineItemDto line, object? rawValue)
    {
        // Same parse + clamp as OnQtyInput.
        if (rawValue is string s && int.TryParse(s, CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, out var parsed))
        {
            var max = GetLineMax(line);
            if (parsed > max) parsed = max;
            SetPendingQty(line.Id, parsed);
        }

        // Only save if the pending qty actually differs from the server's
        // truth. This skips the backend call entirely when the user focused
        // the field and tabbed away without changing anything.
        if (GetPendingQty(line.Id) == line.Quantity) return;

        await HandleUpdateLineAsync(line.Id);
    }

    // ── Display helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Computes the live line total for a cart line, using the user's
    /// pending qty (what they've typed into the qty selector but might not
    /// have committed to the backend yet). Returns UnitPrice × pendingQty
    /// as a new MoneyDto so FormatPrice can render it.
    ///
    /// WHY THIS EXISTS:
    ///   The user wanted real-time price updates as they type, without
    ///   having to click an Update button. line.LineTotal is the SERVER's
    ///   value (based on line.Quantity), which only updates after a backend
    ///   save + reload. Computing from _pendingQuantities gives instant
    ///   feedback on every keystroke.
    /// </summary>
    private MoneyDto ComputeLineTotal(CartLineItemDto line)
    {
        var qty = GetPendingQty(line.Id);
        return new MoneyDto
        {
            Amount = line.UnitPrice.Amount * qty,
            Currency = line.UnitPrice.Currency
        };
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Computes the live cart grand total by summing ComputeLineTotal across
    /// all line items. Uses the line's UnitPrice currency (assumes all lines
    /// share a currency — the backend enforces single-currency carts).
    /// </summary>
    private MoneyDto ComputeCartTotal()
    {
        if (_cart is null || _cart.LineItems.Count == 0)
            return new MoneyDto();

        var total = 0m;
        var currency = _cart.LineItems[0].UnitPrice.Currency;
        foreach (var line in _cart.LineItems)
        {
            total += ComputeLineTotal(line).Amount;
        }
        return new MoneyDto { Amount = total, Currency = currency };
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Computes the live total item count (sum of pending qtys) for the
    /// cart header badge + summary "Total items" row. Uses _pendingQuantities
    /// so the count updates in real time as the user types.
    /// </summary>
    private int ComputeTotalItemCount()
    {
        if (_cart is null) return 0;
        var sum = 0;
        foreach (var line in _cart.LineItems)
        {
            sum += GetPendingQty(line.Id);
        }
        return sum;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// True if any line item has a stock issue — either the product is out
    /// of stock, OR the PENDING qty (what the user has typed but might not
    /// have committed yet) exceeds current stock. Used to:
    ///   - disable the Submit button (defense-in-depth: the backend
    ///     UpdateSaleLineItem/SubmitSale would reject anyway, but disabling
    ///     gives a cleaner UX)
    ///   - show a warning alert above the action buttons
    ///
    /// WHY PENDING QTY (not line.Quantity):
    ///   Before this fix, HasStockIssue used line.Quantity (the server's
    ///   truth), so the Submit button stayed enabled while the user was
    ///   typing an over-stock qty — they'd only see the error on Submit.
    ///   Using the pending qty means the Submit button disables the moment
    ///   the user types an over-stock value, giving instant feedback.
    /// </summary>
    private bool HasStockIssue()
    {
        if (_cart is null) return false;
        foreach (var line in _cart.LineItems)
        {
            var pendingQty = GetPendingQty(line.Id);
            if (line.CurrentStock == 0 || pendingQty > line.CurrentStock)
                return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display. IRR is labelled "ریال" (no division —
    /// the cart shows the real Rial amount the customer will be charged).
    /// Other currencies pass through unchanged.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatPrice(MoneyDto price)
    {
        if (price is null) return "—";
        var isIrr = string.Equals(price.Currency, "IRR", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        var unit = isIrr ? "ریال" : price.Currency;
        return $"{price.Amount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)} {unit}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Translates a backend <c>Result.Error</c> string into a user-facing,
    /// culture-aware message. Returns null if the error doesn't match a
    /// known pattern (the caller should fall back to a generic localized
    /// "something went wrong" message).
    ///
    /// Currently handles:
    ///   - <c>PurchaseLimitExceeded:{name}|{limit}</c> — produced by
    ///     UpdateSaleLineItem / AddItemToSale / CreateOrAppendSale /
    ///     SubmitSale handlers. Localized via the PurchaseLimitExceeded
    ///     resx key, which does NOT mention "groups" (the original
    ///     Persian error leaked the internal group concept to customers).
    ///   - <c>CategoryDeactivated:{productName}</c> — produced by
    ///     UpdateSaleLineItem / AddItemToSale / CreateOrAppendSale /
    ///     SubmitSale handlers when the product's category / sub / sub-sub
    ///     has been deactivated. Localized via the CategoryDeactivated
    ///     resx key. The product's StockQuantity is preserved; only
    ///     visibility + buyability are suppressed.
    ///   - <c>SalaryBudgetExceeded:{productName}|{lineTotal}|{remaining}|{currency}</c>
    ///     — produced by AddItemToSale / UpdateSaleLineItem /
    ///     CreateOrAppendSale / SubmitSale handlers when the salary budget
    ///     (LimitMode = SalaryOnly or Both) would be exceeded by the
    ///     mutation. Localized via the SalaryBudgetExceeded resx key —
    ///     the message NEVER mentions "group" (the customer just sees
    ///     their remaining monthly budget).
    ///   - <c>CurrencyMismatch:{productName}|{productCurrency}|{salaryCurrency}</c>
    ///     — produced by AddItemToSale / UpdateSaleLineItem /
    ///     CreateOrAppendSale / SubmitSale handlers when the product's
    ///     currency doesn't match the customer's salary currency. The
    ///     localized message is intentionally GENERIC ("this item is not
    ///     available for your account") — it does NOT reveal that the
    ///     mismatch is about currency, because that would leak the
    ///     existence of a "salary currency" concept (which implies a
    ///     "group" concept). The customer just sees a polite "not
    ///     available" message with an internal error code for support.
    /// </summary>
    private string? LocalizeError(string? error)
    {
        if (PurchaseLimitErrors.TryParse(error, out var productName, out var limit))
        {
            return string.Format(
                CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                Loc["PurchaseLimitExceeded"],
                productName,
                limit);
        }
        if (CategoryDeactivatedErrors.TryParse(error, out var deactivatedProductName))
        {
            return string.Format(
                CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                Loc["CategoryDeactivated"],
                deactivatedProductName);
        }
        // Step 7 — SalaryBudgetExceeded is produced when the salary budget
        // (LimitMode = SalaryOnly or Both) would be exceeded. The customer
        // sees a friendly message about their remaining monthly budget —
        // the word "group" never appears (per the feature spec).
        if (SalaryBudgetExceededErrors.TryParse(
                error,
                out var sbProductName,
                out var sbLineTotal,
                out var sbRemaining,
                out var sbCurrency))
        {
            // Format the remaining amount using the same Money formatting
            // as the rest of the cart (N0 + "ریال" for IRR, ISO code otherwise).
            var remainingMoney = new MoneyDto
            {
                Amount = Math.Abs(sbRemaining),
                Currency = sbCurrency
            };
            // Negative-prefix when remaining is negative (overdraft — the
            // customer already exceeded their budget before this attempt).
            var remainingDisplay = sbRemaining < 0
                ? $"−{FormatPrice(remainingMoney)}"
                : FormatPrice(remainingMoney);

            return string.Format(
                CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                Loc["SalaryBudgetExceeded"],
                sbProductName,
                remainingDisplay);
        }
        // Step 7 — CurrencyMismatch is produced when the product's currency
        // doesn't match the customer's salary currency. The localized message
        // is intentionally GENERIC — the customer doesn't see the word
        // "currency" or "group", just "this item is not available for your
        // account (code: CurrencyMismatch)". The internal code lets support
        // staff diagnose the issue without leaking the group concept.
        if (CurrencyMismatchErrors.TryParse(error, out _, out _, out _))
        {
            return Loc["CurrencyMismatch"];
        }
        // Stable error code returned by SubmitSaleCommandHandler when the
        // cart is empty — defense-in-depth guard that should never fire
        // (the Submit button is disabled for empty carts, and the
        // QuickReorder handler's compute-first architecture prevents ghost
        // drafts). If it does fire, show a localized message instead of the
        // raw "SubmitEmptyCart" code.
        if (error == "SubmitEmptyCart")
        {
            return Loc["SubmitEmptyCart"];
        }
        return error;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// True if any line item's PENDING quantity exceeds the line's
    /// per-product purchase limit (MyPurchaseLimit). Used to disable the
    /// Submit button + show a warning alert — defense-in-depth on top of
    /// the backend's Submit-time limit check (SubmitSaleCommandHandler).
    ///
    /// Lines where MyPurchaseLimit is null (staff, or no limit set for
    /// this customer's group on this product) are skipped.
    /// </summary>
    private bool HasLimitIssue()
    {
        if (_cart is null) return false;
        foreach (var line in _cart.LineItems)
        {
            if (!line.MyPurchaseLimit.HasValue) continue;
            var pendingQty = GetPendingQty(line.Id);
            if (pendingQty > line.MyPurchaseLimit.Value)
                return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}